{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775255789-CHAiNv9oBHEOlE3En9hy","role":"assistant","created":1775255818,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the structure better. Looking at the data:\n- Line 16: `<td colspan=\"3\">1970</td><td colspan=\"3\">1973</td><td colspan=\"3\">1976</td><td colspan=\"3\">1979</td>` - this is the year header row\n- The monthly data follows, with columns: Month | 1970(1-3) | 1973(4-6) | 1976(7-9) | 1979(10-12)\n\nSo for 1979:\n- Treasury yields are at index 10 (e.g., \"8.43 4/\", \"8.55 4/5/\")\n- Corporate yields are at index 11 (e.g., \"9.47\", \"9.82\")\n\nNow I need to correctly extract the 1979 data (columns 10-11-12 for Treasury/Corporate/Muni).\n\nAlso I noticed there's an issue: my initial approach had some problems. Let me now re-extract correctly for both 1979 and 1984.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_048d2bc7241f6098","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport json\nimport re\nimport math\n\n# Function to calculate Pearson correlation\ndef pearson_correlation(x, y):\n    n = len(x)\n    if n != len(y) or n == 0:\n        return None\n    \n    mean_x = sum(x) / n\n    mean_y = sum(y) / n\n    \n    # Calculate covariance and standard deviations\n    numerator = sum((x[i] - mean_x) * (y[i] - mean_y) for i in range(n))\n    denom_x = sum((x[i] - mean_x) ** 2 for i in range(n))\n    denom_y = sum((y[i] - mean_y) ** 2 for i in range(n))\n    \n    denominator = math.sqrt(denom_x * denom_y)\n    \n    if denominator == 0:\n        return None\n    \n    return numerator / denominator\n\n# ===== EXTRACT 1979 DATA =====\nd1979 = json.load(open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1980_03.json'))\ne1979 = d1979['document']['elements'][966]\ncontent1979 = e1979.get('content', '')\nlines1979 = content1979.split('<tr>')\n\ntreasury_1979 = []\ncorp_1979 = []\nmonths_1979 = []\n\n# Find the row with years and extract monthly data after it\n# We need the section with 1979 - look for \"1979</td>\" in year header\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines1979):\n    if '<td colspan=\"3\">1979</td>' in line:\n        # Found the year header - now extract monthly data from following rows\n        # Monthly data is in lines after this header\n        for j in range(i+1, len(lines1979)):\n            row = lines1979[j]\n            # Check if we've hit another year header (next section)\n            if 'colspan=\"3\">' in row and '197' in row:\n                break\n            \n            # Extract monthly data\n            month_match = re.search(r'<td>(Jan|Feb|Mar|Apr|May|June|July|Aug|Sept|Oct|Nov|Dec)\\.?</td>', row)\n            if month_match:\n                tds = re.findall(r'<td>([^<]*)</td>', row)\n                if len(tds) >= 12:\n                    month = month_match.group(1)\n                    months_1979.append(month)\n                    \n                    # Treasury at index 10, Corporate at index 11\n                    treasury = re.sub(r'\\s*\\d+[/]?.*$', '', tds[10]).strip()\n                    corp = re.sub(r'\\s*\\d+[/]?.*$', '', tds[11]).strip()\n                    \n                    try:\n                        treasury_1979.append(float(treasury))\n                        corp_1979.append(float(corp))\n                    except:\n                        print(f\"Error 1979: {month} - Treasury='{treasury}', Corp='{corp}'\")\n\nprint(\"=== 1979 DATA ===\")\nprint(f\"Months: {months_1979}\")\nprint(f\"Treasury yields: {treasury_1979}\")\nprint(f\"Corporate yields: {corp_1979}\")\nprint(f\"Count: {len(treasury_1979)}\")\n\n# ===== EXTRACT 1984 DATA =====\nd1984 = json.load(open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1985_03.json'))\ne1984 = d1984['document']['elements'][333]\ncontent1984 = e1984.get('content', '')\nlines1984 = content1984.split('<tr>')\n\ntreasury_1984 = []\ncorp_1984 = []\nmonths_1984 = []\n\n# Find the row with years and extract monthly data after it\n# For 1984: 